ONE LINE: kant is being rewritten in kant -- rules whose actions build instructs, on a new road (incant/kantGrammar) beside the old one (incant/grammar) -- and compiled by the jitter rule by rule.

/*****************************************************************************
    Description
*****************************************************************************/
Two roads. The old road is incant/grammar with C++ rule actions; action bodies and forms still parse on it. The new road is incant/kantGrammar: each rule's action is kant and builds an instruct, which runs later.
The jitter compiles a rule through the rule door (jitterRule), one rule per stroke; a compiled rule must answer as the interpreted one does on every row.
A regular rule names its operator (op="...") and the shared default action builds it; no control rule keeps a hand-written action (seal 436).
The design and its reasoning are in IncantForms/WorkingOn/macros ("Kant in kant: the plan").

